        "original_id": "4e69be2c-50e7-5cbd-aa76-5dc6450a5a9a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Denniz Pop\n- Organizations: Cheiron Studios\n- Places: Stockholm, Sweden\n- Products: Earthquake Visions\n- Concepts: Glam metal, funk metal\n- Topics: It's Alive\n\nFacts:\n- It's Alive was a Swedish glam-style funk metal band formed in Stockholm in 1985.\n- Glam metal is a subgenre of heavy metal that features pop-influenced hooks and guitar riffs and borrows from the fashion of 1970s glam rock.\n- Glam metal is also known as hair metal and is often used synonymously with pop metal.\n- In 1994, It's Alive recorded the album Earthquake Visions for Cheiron Studios.",
